rtedNode\ExportedParameterNode":8:{s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀name";s:5:"value";s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀type";s:5:"mixed";s:60:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀byRef";b:0;s:63:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀variadic";b:0;s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀hasDefault";b:0;s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀attributes";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀phpDoc";N;s:60:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀flags";i:0;}}s:62:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀attributes";a:0:{}}}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀attributes";a:0:{}}}a:1:{i:0;O:49:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode":10:{s:55:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀name";s:40:"App\Modules\CRM\Services\GeofenceService";s:57:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀phpDoc";O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode":2:{s:64:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀phpDocString";s:1064:"/**
 * The server's own geofence decision: is the position a device reported good enough, and inside the geofence of a stop
 * on the person's route plan? Nothing the browser or the app computes is trusted — it only sends a position and how
 * accurate it says it is; distance, radius and verdict are worked out here.
 *
 *  - The position must be a real one (latitude −90…90, longitude −180…180, not 0,0) and come with an accuracy.
 *  - The accuracy must be no worse than `geofence.max_accuracy_m`: a reading that could be anywhere within a few
 *    hundred metres says nothing about a 500 m fence.
 *  - Each stop of the plan with a place on the map is a fence: its centre and its radius — the stop's own, else the
 *    plan's, else the company's `geofence.radius_m`. The position qualifies if it is within *any* of them; the stop that
 *    came closest to qualifying is reported either way.
 *
 * It makes the decision and writes nothing: AttendanceService records what came of it (and later the mobile lead-save
 * will reuse it unchanged).
